# OpenSpatialDelay for WebCLAP

OpenSpatialDelay by Spatial Media Lab (Andrew Rahman), a spatial delay whose echoes are placed and moved in 3D space,
ported to WebCLAP. This is not an official OpenSpatialDelay release.

- OpenSpatialDelay: https://github.com/Spatial-Media-Lab/OpenSpatialDelay (commit 14947a0, version 1.0.0)
- This port, and the complete source of this bundle: @SOURCE_URL@
  Build it with `scripts/build-open-spatial-delay.sh`, which fetches every dependency below at the commit named here.

Changes in this port (`patches/open-spatial-delay-webclap.patch`): a stereo output bus, no OSC (a page has no
UDP), and three of the five HRTF sets. The SADIE II and Bernschütz KU100 sets (profiles Immersive and Spatial) are
left out for size, a project that uses them gets the Simple renderer with that profile's head model, as upstream does
when a set fails to load.

